---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CTA from "@/components/sections/CTA.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Viona is the AI video editor for every kind of video. Describe the edit you want in plain English — Viona performs it."
>
  <section class="pt-32 pb-20 lg:pt-40">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">
          About <span class="text-brand">Viona</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
          Viona is the AI video editor for every kind of video. Describe the edit you want in
          plain English, and Viona performs it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="space-y-12">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">The Problem</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Video is the most effective medium online — and the most expensive one to produce.
            Every video, whether it's a YouTube essay, a product demo, a tutorial, a vlog, or a
            launch film, demands the same grind: rough cut, trim filler, add captions, color,
            graphics, re-export for each platform. Most of that work isn't creative. It's
            mechanical. And it's exactly the kind of work AI should handle.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Our Solution</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Viona is an AI co-editor you direct in plain English. Cut the first 30 seconds.
            Remove the ums. Make the captions MrBeast style. Add a bar chart when I mention the
            three metrics. Re-export for TikTok. Each prompt maps to a concrete edit, and the
            AI performs it in seconds. You review, refine, ship.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">The Technology</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
            At the core of Viona is a pipeline that does three things most editors don't combine:
            word-level transcription, semantic scene understanding, and an LLM agent that
            translates natural-language instructions into timeline operations. Together they let
            you direct edits the way you'd direct a human editor — "tighten the opening",
            "swap the caption style", "regenerate this visual in a cleaner layout" — and have
            the software actually do it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Because the model reads your transcript at the word level, every edit — cuts, caption
            timing, visual placement — stays frame-accurate even after you rearrange the video.
            When visuals help, Viona generates them: flowcharts for processes, charts for data,
            step sequences for walk-throughs, all timed to the word they're referenced on. When
            they don't, they stay out of the way.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Who We Help</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Anyone shipping video. Short-form creators publishing to TikTok, Reels, and Shorts.
            YouTubers editing long-form essays, vlogs, and tutorials. Educators and course
            creators turning lectures into polished lessons. Marketing and product teams
            producing launch videos, demos, webinar clips, and social cut-downs at volume.
            Agencies shipping a week's worth of client work in a day.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            The common thread: you'd rather describe the edit than perform it. You want the AI
            to handle the mechanical 80% so you can spend your time on the creative 20%.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">How It Works</h2>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Upload your video. Viona transcribes it at the word level and builds a scene model
            of what's happening. You prompt the edits you want — cuts, caption style, aspect
            ratio, visuals, color, pacing — and Viona performs them. Review each change, accept
            or refine, and export to every platform you publish on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Our Principles</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-medium mb-2">Prompt-first, not timeline-first</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                Traditional editors put a timeline in front of you and ask you to perform every
                operation by hand. Viona puts a conversation in front of you. You describe what
                you want, and the software handles the mechanics. The timeline is still there
                when you want it — but it's no longer the only way to work.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-medium mb-2">Creator in control</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                Every edit is reviewable, reversible, and refinable. The AI is a co-editor, not a
                black box. You can always see what it did, undo it, or ask for something
                different. No prompt is one-shot, and no change is permanent until you ship.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-medium mb-2">Every kind of video</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                We don't build for a single format or audience. Talking heads, vlogs, tutorials,
                demos, interviews, podcast clips, launch films, montages — they all benefit from
                the same core operations, and Viona ships them for all of them. The right visual
                system for your video is the one you choose, not the one we force.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-medium mb-2">Accessible by default</h3>
              <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
                You shouldn't need to learn After Effects or Premiere Pro to ship a polished
                video. If you can record yourself and describe the edit you want, you have
                everything you need. Captions, filler-word removal, and multi-format export ship
                in every plan because they're the baseline, not a premium tier.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
